{
  "window_id": "w0021",
  "observed_failures": [
    {
      "filename": "034.jpg",
      "field": "date",
      "predicted": "2018-08-09",
      "visible_on_receipt": "Date: 09/03/2018",
      "symptom": "OCR misread day/month digits; '03' read as '08' or month/day swap; no cross-validation across OCR passes."
    },
    {
      "filename": "074.jpg",
      "field": "total_amount",
      "predicted": "702.00",
      "visible_on_receipt": "Subtotal 102.00 / Total incl. of GST 102.00 / Total Amt Rounded 102.00 / Payment 102.00",
      "symptom": "Agent took last candidate on a keyword line where OCR mangled '102.00' into '702.00' ('1' confused with '7'); no consensus with repeated 102.00 elsewhere on receipt."
    },
    {
      "filename": "077.jpg",
      "field": "total_amount",
      "predicted": "23.26",
      "visible_on_receipt": "Total (Inclusive of GST): 23.26, Rounding Adj: -0.01, TOTAL: 23.25",
      "symptom": "Priority tier matched 'Total (Inclusive of GST)' before the bold rounded 'TOTAL' line; the final rounded TOTAL (23.25) was ignored."
    },
    {
      "filename": "078.jpg",
      "field": "total_amount",
      "predicted": "",
      "visible_on_receipt": "Total: 92.80 / Grand Total: 92.80 / Cash Received 100.00 / Change 7.20",
      "symptom": "Extraction failed and agent wrote empty string instead of real null; the receipt clearly contains a TOTAL/GRAND TOTAL line so extraction should not have failed under the documented priority."
    }
  ],
  "root_causes": [
    "image-ocr priority tiers conflate 'Total (Inclusive of GST)' and 'Rounded TOTAL': both match the generic TOTAL tier, and the current rule 'prefer earliest' or 'prefer a specific tier' picks the pre-rounding value when the final TOTAL appears later.",
    "Amount extraction relies on a single OCR candidate per line with no cross-check against other high-signal lines on the same receipt (subtotal, cash, payment, rounded total). OCR digit confusions (1/7, 0/O, 8/3) therefore propagate directly to the output.",
    "Date extraction runs on a single OCR pass with no voting across preprocessing variants; a single mis-OCR'd digit silently produces a wrong but parseable ISO date.",
    "The output writer does not enforce None-vs-empty-string: when per-field extraction returned None the agent wrote '' into the cell, which is scored as incorrect and is explicitly warned against in the current xlsx skill but not enforced via a verification step.",
    "Fallback 'last number on keyword line' has no sanity filter: it will accept a heavily mangled number ('——S«702.00') that disagrees with other copies of the same amount elsewhere on the receipt."
  ],
  "skill_defects": [
    {
      "skill": "image-ocr",
      "defect": "TOTAL_PRIORITY tiers do not include an explicit 'rounded/final total' tier (e.g., 'TOTAL AFTER ROUNDING', 'TOTAL ROUNDED', 'ROUNDED TOTAL', 'GRAND TOTAL' after a rounding-adjustment line) above the generic 'Total (Inclusive of GST)' / 'Net Total' matches."
    },
    {
      "skill": "image-ocr",
      "defect": "extract_total selects a single candidate without any within-receipt corroboration. There is no guidance to collect all monetary candidates with 2 decimals and prefer the value that is repeated (e.g., Subtotal == Total == Payment)."
    },
    {
      "skill": "image-ocr",
      "defect": "Multi-pass OCR pattern is described but not applied to structured extraction: the skill does not say 'run both default-PSM and preprocessed OCR, extract (tier, value) from each, and vote', which is the exact pattern needed for OCR digit-confusion cases."
    },
    {
      "skill": "image-ocr",
      "defect": "Date extraction section does not require cross-pass agreement and does not note that DD/MM vs MM/DD ambiguity plus single-digit OCR errors (e.g., '03'→'08') must be defended against by voting across passes or by preferring dates that also appear in a secondary location on the receipt."
    },
    {
      "skill": "xlsx",
      "defect": "Strict-Schema Outputs section warns against empty strings but provides no concrete pre-write normalization step (e.g., replace '', 'None', 'NaN', 'nan' with None) and no post-write assertion that empty cells are truly empty, not ''. The failure on 078.jpg is exactly this pattern."
    },
    {
      "skill": "xlsx",
      "defect": "No guidance that extraction-pipeline None values must bubble through pandas without being coerced to NaN strings when writing via ExcelWriter; the canonical pattern does not include a `df.where(df.notna(), None)` or equivalent safety net."
    }
  ],
  "repair_recommendations": [
    {
      "skill": "image-ocr",
      "change": "Introduce a top-priority tier for post-rounding/final totals that must be tried before generic 'TOTAL'/'AMOUNT' matches: patterns like r'TOTAL\\s*(AFTER\\s*)?ROUND(ED|ING)?', r'ROUNDED\\s*TOTAL', r'TOTAL\\s*AMT\\s*ROUNDED', and prefer the LAST occurrence of 'TOTAL' when a 'ROUNDING ADJ' line appears above it. Document that on receipts with both 'Total (Inclusive of GST)' and a later bold 'TOTAL' the later one wins."
    },
    {
      "skill": "image-ocr",
      "change": "Add a 'within-receipt corroboration' step for total extraction: collect every candidate line's (tier, value) across ALL keyword matches (including payment/cash/rounded-total/subtotal) and, when the top tier yields a value that does NOT appear anywhere else in the receipt text, prefer a tied-or-lower-tier value that is repeated at least twice. This defends against single-line OCR digit errors (1/7, 0/8)."
    },
    {
      "skill": "image-ocr",
      "change": "Promote the existing multi-pass OCR pattern from a nice-to-have into the documented pipeline for structured receipt extraction: run default PSM and preprocessed+PSM6 passes, extract (tier, value) from each, prefer higher-priority tier; on tier tie, prefer agreement; on disagreement with equal priority, prefer the candidate that has exactly 2 decimal digits and appears elsewhere on the receipt. Include a short pseudocode block, not a full implementation."
    },
    {
      "skill": "image-ocr",
      "change": "Harden date extraction: require at least one of (a) the same ISO date to parse from two OCR variants, or (b) the day/month/year to each individually appear in >=2 passes. If no corroboration is possible, prefer returning None over a single-pass guess. Add explicit note that DD/MM/YYYY is the default ordering for the receipt domain and MM/DD/YYYY must not be attempted first."
    },
    {
      "skill": "image-ocr",
      "change": "Expand the number regex guidance: monetary totals MUST have exactly 2 decimal digits (reject 'XX.X' and bare integers) and must not be preceded/followed by a digit. Explicitly warn that candidates with adjacent OCR noise (non-ascii, consecutive punctuation like '——S«', trailing letters) should be down-weighted or skipped when a cleaner candidate of equal priority exists."
    },
    {
      "skill": "xlsx",
      "change": "Add a required pre-write normalization step to the Strict-Schema Outputs canonical pattern: convert '', 'None', 'none', 'NaN', 'nan', and pandas NA to Python None for every cell before `to_excel`, e.g. `df = df.where(pd.notna(df), None); df = df.replace({'': None, 'None': None, 'NaN': None, 'nan': None})`. Make this step MANDATORY, not optional, and show it in the canonical snippet."
    },
    {
      "skill": "xlsx",
      "change": "Add a post-write verification assertion that for every column the set of 'missing' cells is exactly those where the source row had None; specifically, re-open the file and assert that no cell contains the string '' or 'nan'. Include this in the verification checklist and in the canonical example."
    },
    {
      "skill": "xlsx",
      "change": "Clarify that when a per-row processing function returns None for a field, callers MUST propagate None end-to-end (not '' or 'null' or 'N/A'). Add this as a bullet in the Pitfalls list referencing the extraction-row pattern already shown in image-ocr."
    }
  ],
  "confidence": "medium-high"
}
